# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the SFTP tests:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/sftp/tsan.supp
#
# QtCore isn't built with ThreadSanitizer, so it can't see the locking Qt
# does when it hands work between threads. Our own data crosses threads
# through SftpWorker's std::mutex queue, which TSan does see. What's left
# are two hand-offs entirely inside Qt:
#  - the shared state of a QFuture, created on the UI thread and released
#    on the worker when its QPromise finishes (reference-counted in QtCore);
#  - the queued call that wakes the worker, created by QMetaObject::
#    invokeMethod on the UI thread and run on the worker via the event
#    queue (locked in QtCore).
# Keep these entries this narrow, so real races in our code still show.
race:QMetaTypeForType<QFutureInterface<void>>::getDtor
race:QCallableObject<void (SftpWorker::*)()
